  "worked_solution": "Since we are given both the derivative of the curve ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ and the derivative of the unit tangent ${T}^{\u2032}(t)$, we will use the following formula for the curvature:\n\n$$\n\u03ba(t)=\\frac{\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}\n$$\n\nNow, we find the magnitudes of ${r}^{\u2032}(t)$ and ${T}^{\u2032}(t):$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{{1}^{2}+{(-\\frac{t}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{1+\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4-{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{4-{t}^{2}+{t}^{2}}{4-{t}^{2}}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}} \\\\ \u2016{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016 & =\\sqrt{{(-\\frac{t}{2\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}})}^{2}+{(-\\frac{1}{2})}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{t}^{2}}{4(4-{t}^{2})}+\\frac{1}{4}} \\\\  & =\\sqrt{\\frac{{t}^{2}+4-{t}^{2}}{4(4-{t}^{2})}} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the curvature is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\u03ba(t) & =\\frac{\u2016{T}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}{\u2016{r}^{\u2032}(t)\u2016}=\\frac{(\\frac{1}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}})}{(\\frac{2}{\\sqrt{4-{t}^{2}}})}=\\frac{1}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
